# Advance the epistemic state by one executed action.
#
# The action is named in the task's own vocabulary — the grounded name the
# planner searched over, which travels on PlanItem.epistemic_action. Applying
# it performs the DEL product update, which is what makes the executor's model
# of what the agents know follow what they actually did.
string epistemic_action

# For a sensing action, the outcome the robot observed, named by the event that
# fired. Leave empty to let the model decide: when the state designates a
# single world the outcome is determined and the response reports it. When it
# does not, the model genuinely cannot know, and an observation is required
# rather than guessed.
string observed_outcome

# What to do when the observation contradicts the model: when the action is not
# applicable, or the observed outcome is not one it could produce here.
#
# False refuses the update and leaves the model as it was. That keeps the model
# honest about never having represented what happened, but it also freezes it:
# a replan from a state that refused an observation starts from the belief the
# observation just contradicted, and plans for a world that has been ruled out.
#
# True repairs it instead, by trusting the observation over the belief. The
# model is re-designated to the worlds where the observed event could have
# fired, and the update proceeds from there. This is a real change of belief
# and not a correction of arithmetic, so the response says when it happened and
# the state says so in its log.
#
# Recovery is possible only when some world in the model could have produced
# the observation. When none could, the model cannot represent what happened at
# all and the update is refused whatever this says.
bool allow_recovery
---
bool success
string error

# True when the update went through only because the model was repaired first.
# A caller that cares whether its belief has been overridden reads this; one
# that does not still gets a working state.
bool recovered

# What the model had to give up, when it was repaired. Empty otherwise.
string recovery

# The outcome that occurred, for a sensing action: either the observation that
# was passed in, or the one the model determined. Empty for an ontic action,
# whose effect does not depend on an observation.
string outcome

# The state after the update, for the caller to log or display.
uint32 num_worlds
uint32 num_designated
